~ rag_1

Hero: That gate won't open for wishing. Something in here might help. [ID:HINT_RAG_1]

=> END

~ rag_2

Hero: There's a rag on a hook by the wall. Rags are rarely useless. [ID:HINT_RAG_2]

=> END

~ word_1

Hero: The gatekeeper wants a word. Words have to come from somewhere. [ID:HINT_WORD_1]

=> END

~ word_2

Hero: The chapel's altar. Its past might remember what its present forgot. [ID:HINT_WORD_2]

=> END

~ oil_1

Hero: Those hinges are rusted solid. They need something to drink. [ID:HINT_OIL_1]

=> END

~ oil_2

Hero: There's a flask on the chapel shelf. [ID:HINT_OIL_2]

=> END

~ hinges_1

Hero: Oil and a rag. Together they might do what neither does alone. [ID:HINT_HINGES_1]

=> END

~ hinges_2

Hero: Combine the oil with the rag, then use it on the gate. [ID:HINT_HINGES_2]

=> END

~ say_word_1

Hero: The gate is ready. The gatekeeper is still waiting for the word. [ID:HINT_SAY_WORD_1]

=> END

~ through_1

Hero: The gate is open. Whatever is beyond it is waiting. [ID:HINT_THROUGH_1]

=> END

~ none

Hero: Nothing pulls at me right now. [ID:HINT_NONE_1]

=> END
